# esbuild - resolved by a version override, kept as a record.
#
# drizzle-kit pins esbuild ^0.25.x, and that is still true at 1.0.0-rc.4. The
# 0.25.x line was abandoned after 0.25.12 (Nov 2025), a binary built on
# go1.23.12 carrying 22 findings including one CRITICAL, so waiting for a
# drizzle release was never going to clear it - drizzle-orm#5481 has been open
# and unanswered since March 2026.
#
# The esbuild override in pnpm-workspace.yaml now forces a single 0.28.2
# (go1.26.5) across the tree, which is why the ids that used to be listed here
# are gone rather than suppressed. That override also keeps the abandoned
# @esbuild-kit/core-utils pin (esbuild ~0.18.20, GHSA-67mh-4wv8-2f99) out of
# the tree entirely - do not relax it below 0.28.2.
#
# Seven Go stdlib CVEs are still genuinely unfixed at go1.26.5 and need
# go1.26.6 or newer:
#   CVE-2026-33818  CVE-2026-39821  CVE-2026-56853  CVE-2026-56858
#   CVE-2026-56859  CVE-2026-56860  CVE-2026-56862
#
# They are deliberately NOT ignored below. Trivy cannot read build info out of
# the 0.28.2 binary, so it reports nothing for them today; and these are stdlib
# ids that apply to any Go binary, so a blanket ignore would also mask them if
# they ever showed up somewhere else in the image. They clear on the first
# esbuild release built with Go 1.27 (released 2026-08-19).
